{"name":"Rosebud Tea","hex":"#eec6c3","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rosebud","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The bud of a rose.","A pretty young woman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rosebud"},{"term":"tea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Temiar."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The tea plant (Camellia sinensis);  a variety of this plant.","The dried leaves or buds of the tea plant;  a variety of such leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosebud (Fabergé egg)","blocks":[{"text":"The Rosebud egg is a jewelled enameled Easter egg made by Michael Perchin under the supervision of the Russian jeweller Peter Carl Fabergé in 1895, for Nicholas II of Russia, who presented the egg to his wife, Empress Alexandra Feodorovna. It was the first Fabergé egg that Nicholas presented to Alexandra."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rosebud_egg.jpg/330px-Rosebud_egg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosebud_(Faberg%C3%A9_egg)","wikidata":"Q4536589"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rosebud_egg.jpg/500px-Rosebud_egg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped